Keeps `.github/` in git, because git does not track empty directories.

`legacy-billing` is the unsafe fixture and the `no_ci` ground-truth entry
cites `.github`: the directory exists, and there is no workflow in it. On a
fresh clone the directory vanished entirely, the citation stopped resolving,
and the measured hallucination rate went 0.000 -> 0.083, failing the eval
gate. Green in the working copy, red in a clean checkout.

This marker lives in `.github/` rather than `.github/workflows/` on purpose.
`repo_stats` detects CI with `r.startswith(".github/workflows/")`, so a
placeholder one level deeper would have made `has_ci` report **true** for
the repository whose entire job is to have no CI - fixing the clone bug by
silently corrupting the fixture.

Do not move this file into `workflows/`, and do not add a workflow beside it.
